meta {
  name: Update a person
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

put {
  url: {{host}}/api/persons/{{personId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Example Scope Admin, renamed",
    "email": "scope.admin@example.com"
  }
}

docs {
  UC-08. Any authenticated caller, subject to the handler's rules.

  roleId may only be changed by a System Admin; omit it entirely for a self-service name and email edit, which is what this body does.

  Changing your own email also needs "currentPassword", and "twoFactorCode" (an app or email code, or a recovery code) when your two-factor authentication is active; either missing or wrong answers 401. An administrator changing someone else's email sends neither. Any email change revokes the person's tokens, so after changing your own, sign in again.
}
